# Code owners — automatically requested as reviewers on every pull request.
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# An entry that does not resolve to a collaborator with write access is
# ignored silently: no review is requested and nothing warns you. Keep this
# file in step with the repository's actual collaborators.
#
# @Dashmake-Startup/maintainers holds write access on this repository and
# contains the seven members of the organisation. Both facts have to stay true:
# the team losing repository access, or a member leaving the team, is reported
# nowhere — the rule just quietly stops requesting reviews.
#
# A team named as code owner is requested as a whole; one approval from any of
# its members satisfies the rule.

# Default.
* @Dashmake-Startup/maintainers

# Tooling, CI and governance — deliberately narrower.
/.github/                 @KevinAkpe
/electron-builder.yml     @KevinAkpe
/electron.vite.config.ts  @KevinAkpe
/package.json             @KevinAkpe
/package-lock.json        @KevinAkpe
/tsconfig*.json           @KevinAkpe
/eslint.config.*          @KevinAkpe
/.husky/                  @KevinAkpe

# Security-sensitive: main process, preload surface, native bridge.
/src/main/      @KevinAkpe
/src/preload/   @KevinAkpe
